; Print the relation word of a holder
;
; Prints the 4-byte message at #R$AFCA + 4 * (state & 15), where the state is the
; low nibble of the holder's state byte (+4): how the holder keeps what is in
; it. The table starts "In the", "On the", "Behind the", "Under the", "Tied
; to the". Used before the name of a container in "<In the> chest: ..." lines.
; The message is printed by a jump to #R$72DD.
;
; IX Record of the holder
@label=PrintHolderRelation
c$A09D LD HL,$AFCA
 $A0A0 LD A,(IX+$04)    ; state byte (+4)
 $A0A3 RLCA             ; rotate twice and mask: (state & 15) * 4
 $A0A4 RLCA
 $A0A5 AND $3C
 $A0A7 LD E,A
 $A0A8 LD D,$00
 $A0AA ADD HL,DE
 $A0AB JP $72DD         ; print and return
